    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nSherry FitzGerald Crowley are delighted to bring to the market this magnificent four bedroom architecturally designed detached bungalow, tucked away in a secluded setting of natural beauty, commanding wonderful countryside and mountain views, on an extensive site of approximately 8.8 acres. \n\nBuilt in 2006 to an exacting standard, this property comes to the market in turnkey condition throughout. With a total floor area of approximately 220sqm/2,368 sq ft, accommodation comprises of a entrance hallway, a spacious, light filled kitchen/dining room with full length sliding doors onto the patio area, creating a connection between the indoor and outdoor living space. A cosy living room with a small office that could easily be used for additional storage, study or a bar area is just off the kitchen. The long hallway offers an abundance of storage with built in soft touch tall boy units integrated into the space. \n\nThere are four spacious double bedrooms, two which benefit from en-suites and the master bedroom offers a fully shelved walk-in wardrobe and a jack and Jill bathroom with a bath, situated beside a picture window offering countryside views. One of the most exciting features of this modern home is the indoor wellness room complete with a resistance pool for year-round fitness and a yoga/relaxation space. \n\nAdjoining the property is a workshop (227.8sqft) which acts as a plant room for the Ground Source Heat Pump and excellent storage space. There is also an integrated garage (161.95sq ft) with a roller door and electricity. \n\nCombining thoughtful design, extensive storage and exceptional features, this is a contemporary home designed equally for comfortable modern family living and suitable for both entertaining guests and relaxation\n\nGarden\n\nThe home is surrounded by stunning countryside and mountain views, available from all corners of the 8.8 acres. \n\nThis property is a gardener's paradise accessed via a mature tree lined avenue, onto a gravel driveway with ample parking and bordered by hand built local stone walls. \n\nWell-manicured green hedges divide the garden into a number of enclosed private sections, including a small patio, and some vegetable patches for those aspiring to be self-sufficient. \n\nThere are apple & plum trees as well as blueberries, blackcurrant and redcurrant bushes. \nThe main area of the site which is to the front has extensive planting of trees and shrubbery. \n\nThe garden also offers a series of walkways through this area, creating peaceful routes in and around the surrounding trees as far as the man-made pond to the front of the site\nTo the side of the property is a block shed that has been divided up into a dry woodshed, storage and a greenhouse. \n\nLocation.\n\nGortnaheltia is an attractive countryside area within a ten minute drive of Newport town and approximately 20 minutes from Westport. Glenhest National School and Church are a 1.3km from the property.\n\nNewport town's amenities including primary school, shops, restaurants/bars, hotel and Newport Harbour at the mouth of Clew Bay. \n\nNewport sits along the popular Great Western Greenway cycle and walking trail that runs from Westport town to Achill Island and has many leisure facilities on its doorstep"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nEntrance Hall - 4.15m x 1.75m\nTiled floor, feature pocket shelves, built in tall boy units\n\nKitchen/Dining Room - 8.2m x 4.4m\nTiled floor, matt slab kitchen, Iroko countertop, tall storage units, mosaic backsplash, eye level oven, induction hob, glass shelving, feature drop lights, fridge freezer, double slide doors to garden with external electric roller shutter doors\n\nLiving Room - 5.3m x 4.3m & 1.87m x 1.86m\nYarrawood flooring, solid fuel stove with brushed concrete plinth, feature recessed shelving, office nook, velux windows\n\nUtility Room & Wet Room - 2.65m x 2.65m & 2m x 1.3m\nTiled floor, built in units, solid timber worktop, plumbed washer/dryer, shower, wc\n\nHallway - 11.7m x 1.21m\nTiled floor, ample tall boy soft touch built in units, shelving\n\nBedroom One - 4.5m x 3m\nTiled floor, built in wardrobe, floating bedside shelf, blinds\n\nEn-Suite - 1.52m x 1.3m & 0.82m x 0.65m\nFully tiled, shower, floating sink, wc\n\nBedroom Two - 5.45m x 2.95m\nTiled floor, floating bedside shelf, blinds\n\nEn-Suite - 1.52m x 1.3m & 0.82m x 0.65m\nTiled floor, shower, floating sink, wc\n\nBedroom Three - 4.1m x 2.95m\nTiled floor, blinds\n\nWalk in Wardrobe - 2.3m x 1.85m\nTiled floor, pull out shelving, box shelving, shoe racks, hanging rails\n\nJack & Jill En-Suite - 2.9m x 2.47m\nFully tiled, wet room shower, bath (good countryside views), floating whb, wc, velux\n\nBedroom Four - 4.5m x 3.17m\nTiled floor, built in wardrobes, floating beside shelf, blinds\n\nPool/Gym Area - 9.35m x 3.72m\nTiled floor, resistance pool, velux windows\n\nPool Plant Room - 1.55m x 1.3m\nOwn electricity supply\n\n"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "<ul><li>Four bedroom architecturally designed home, completed to an exceptionally high standard</li><li>Quiet and peaceful location on a site of approximately 8.8acres</li><li>Ground source heat pump, Heat recovery system and solid fuel stove</li><li>Double glazed windows & doors and Roller shutter doors</li><li>Wellness room with a resistance pool and yoga/relaxation space</li><li>Fibre Broadband</li><li>Less than 10 minutes drive from Newport town and all its amenities</li><li>Westport and Castlebar Towns are within a 30 minute drive</ul>"
